    "https://www.presby.edu/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/employment/adjunct-instructor-french/": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor of",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - French | Presbyterian College Skip to content Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Apply Info Visit Give Open\r\n                            Search Search for: Open Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Admissions Admissions Why PC First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Graduate Students Visit Us Academics Academics at PC Majors, Minors, & Special Programs Academic Resources Civil Conversations Heart of Service Center for Inquiry, Research & Scholarship Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Student Life Student Life Get Involved Health & Wellness Living on Campus Spiritual Life Career & Professional Development Blue Hose Athletics Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Affordability Scholarships Grants Loans FAFSA Net Price Calculator Student Employment Tuition & Fees Veteran Benefits About PC About Presbyterian College Leadership History, Mission & Plan Justice & Community Wellbeing For The Community Governance & Policies Accreditation Offices & Services News Giving Events FAQs Athletics Directory Alumni Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Adjunct Instructor of French Adjunct Instructor of French About PC Offices & Services Human Resources Employment Adjunct Instructor – French Adjunct Instructor of French Position Overview The Department of Modern Foreign Languages at Presbyterian College invites applications for an adjunct instructor to teach beginning and intermediate courses in French, starting in Fall semester 2026. The possibility of teaching an upper-level course could apply to candidates with sufficient qualifications and experience. Applicants must have at least 18 credit hours of graduate work completed in French or a related field or certification to teach French at the collegiate level. The ideal candidate will be able to teach 1-2 three-credit courses per semester. The courses would preferably be taught in-person, though teaching online courses is acceptable as well. Candidates must reside in the state of South Carolina to be considered for the position. To Apply Interested individuals should provide a curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts from all graduate institutions, and three references with contact information. Materials should be sent electronically to the Provost, Dr. Erin McAdams, at [email protected] . Please contact Dr. Patrick Kiley , program director of French, if you have any questions about the position. About Presbyterian College Presbyterian College (PC) is a liberal arts college affiliated with the Presbyterian Church USA. The college is committed to an equitable and inclusive learning environment for all students, supports academic freedom, and encourages community involvement. Located in Clinton, South Carolina, PC is approximately 40 minutes from Greenville and Spartanburg, South Carolina and about one hour from Columbia, South Carolina. The region offers abundant opportunity for social and recreational activities, with easy access to Asheville and Charlotte, North Carolina, and Atlanta, Georgia. Presbyterian College is an EEO employer and does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status or genetic information. PC is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from minorities and women. Learn More About PC About PC History, Mission, & Plan Benefits & Resources Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: 503 South Broad Street Clinton, South Carolina 29325 800.476.7272 Contact Us facebook instagram x flickr Quick Links & Resources Quick Links & Resources News Events Directory Athletics Campus Map Living on Campus Academic Calendar Course Catalog Offices & Facilities Accreditation Job Opportunities Justice & Community Wellbeing First-Gen Students International Students Accessible Education Health & Wellness Single-Sign On BannerWeb Brightspace Campus Bookstore Library Online Payment Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: © Copyright 2026 Presbyterian College | Title IX Policies Consumer Information Campus Police Presbyterian College is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive online experience. If you are unable to access any part of this website due to a disability, please contact Accessible Education at [email protected] for assistance. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATORY POLICY AS TO STUDENTS: Presbyterian College is an equal educational opportunity institution. The College’s admission standards and practices are free from discrimination on the basis of age, sex, race, creed, color, disability, ethnicity or national origin. Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community"
    },
    "https://www.presby.edu/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/employment/assistant-professor-of-accounting/": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Accounting | Presbyterian College Skip to content Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Apply Info Visit Give Open\r\n                            Search Search for: Open Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Admissions Admissions Why PC First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Graduate Students Visit Us Academics Academics at PC Majors, Minors, & Special Programs Academic Resources Civil Conversations Heart of Service Center for Inquiry, Research & Scholarship Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Student Life Student Life Get Involved Health & Wellness Living on Campus Spiritual Life Career & Professional Development Blue Hose Athletics Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Affordability Scholarships Grants Loans FAFSA Net Price Calculator Student Employment Tuition & Fees Veteran Benefits About PC About Presbyterian College Leadership History, Mission & Plan Justice & Community Wellbeing For The Community Governance & Policies Accreditation Offices & Services News Giving Events FAQs Athletics Directory Alumni Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Assistant Professor of Accounting Assistant Professor of Accounting About PC Offices & Services Human Resources Employment Assistant Professor of Accounting Assistant Professor of Accounting Position Description The Department of Economics and Business Administration at Presbyterian College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Accounting, starting in Fall 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to high-quality undergraduate teaching, active student engagement, and exceptional service to the department and college community. Teaching Teach undergraduate accounting courses, including but not limited to Intermediate Accounting, Accounting Information Systems, Auditing, and Federal Income Taxation Advise and mentor students pursuing careers in accounting and related business fields to foster their intellectual and professional growth Support activities that strengthen relationships with the accounting profession, including internships, career preparation, and employer partnerships Contribute to departmental and college-wide initiatives through committee service Minimum Requirements Ph.D. in Accounting, or a Master’s degree in Accounting from an AACSB accredited institution Active Certified Public Accountant (CPA) license Significant professional accounting experience in public, corporate, governmental, or nonprofit accounting Preferred Qualifications Previous college or university teaching experience Experience integrating accounting technologies and enterprise software into instruction Familiarity with current accounting information systems, auditing technologies, and data analytics applications Experience advising students or mentoring aspiring accounting professionals Evidence of professional engagement through continuing education, professional organizations, or scholarly activity To Apply Interested individuals should electronically send a single PDF containing a cover letter that describes your motivation for applying for this position; curriculum vitae ; statement of teaching philosophy; evidence of active CPA licensure; three letters of recommendation; and (official or unofficial) college and graduate transcripts to Provost Dr. Erin McAdams at [email protected] . Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. For specific questions regarding the position, please contact Professor Karen Mattison, MAcc, CPA, chair of the Economics and Business Administration department, at [email protected] . About Presbyterian College Presbyterian College (PC) is a liberal arts college affiliated with the Presbyterian Church USA. The college is committed to an equitable and inclusive learning environment for all students, supports academic freedom, and encourages community involvement.  Located in Clinton, South Carolina, PC is approximately 40 minutes from Greenville and Spartanburg, South Carolina and about one hour from Columbia, South Carolina. The region offers abundant opportunity for social and recreational activities, with easy access to Asheville and Charlotte, North Carolina, and Atlanta, Georgia. Presbyterian College is an EEO employer and does not discriminate against any person or group on the basis of age, color, disability, gender, pregnancy, national origin, race, religion, sexual orientation, veteran status or genetic information.  PC is building a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment and encourages applications from minorities and women. Learn More About PC About PC History, Mission, & Plan Benefits & Resources Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: 503 South Broad Street Clinton, South Carolina 29325 800.476.7272 Contact Us facebook instagram x flickr Quick Links & Resources Quick Links & Resources News Events Directory Athletics Campus Map Living on Campus Academic Calendar Course Catalog Offices & Facilities Accreditation Job Opportunities Justice & Community Wellbeing First-Gen Students International Students Accessible Education Health & Wellness Single-Sign On BannerWeb Brightspace Campus Bookstore Library Online Payment Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: © Copyright 2026 Presbyterian College | Title IX Policies Consumer Information Campus Police Presbyterian College is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive online experience. If you are unable to access any part of this website due to a disability, please contact Accessible Education at [email 