    "https://www.presby.edu/about/offices-and-services/human-resources/": {
      "title": "Human Resources",
      "description": "Human Resources | Presbyterian College Skip to content Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Apply Info Visit Give Open\r\n                            Search Search for: Open Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Admissions Admissions Why PC First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Admitted Students Graduate Students Visit Us Academics Academics at PC Majors, Minors, & Special Programs Academic Resources Civil Conversations Heart of Service Center for Inquiry, Research & Scholarship Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Student Life Student Life Get Involved Health & Wellness Living on Campus Spiritual Life Career & Professional Development Blue Hose Athletics Cost & Aid Cost & Aid Affordability Scholarships Grants Loans FAFSA Net Price Calculator Student Employment Tuition & Fees Veteran Benefits About PC About Presbyterian College Leadership History, Mission & Plan Justice & Community Wellbeing For The Community Governance & Policies Accreditation Offices & Services News Giving Events FAQs Athletics Directory Alumni Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Human Resources Human Resources Human Resources Human Resources About PC Offices & Services Human Resources LIVE TRUE BLUE: WHERE SERVICE MEETS PURPOSE AND POTENTIAL At Presbyterian College, you’ll become part of a community where service forms the foundation of everything we do. Our motto “While we live, we serve” guides our approach to education and community support, creating an environment where you can make a meaningful impact on students’ lives. Working here means joining a supportive True Blue community of colleagues who share your commitment to transforming students in mind, heart, and spirit. We support Presbyterian College’s strategic goals to foster a work environment where every employee can thrive as True Blue members of our community. We are dedicated to providing exceptional human resources services to attract, develop, and retain top talent while cultivating a people-first culture that empowers individuals to reach their highest potential. Human Resources Employment Benefits & Resources New Hire Onboarding Employment at PC PC offers more than just a job—it’s an opportunity to contribute to an enduring legacy dating back to 1880. You’ll thrive in a workplace that values bold ideas, resourcefulness, and proactive problem-solving while helping empower the next generation of innovators, service leaders, and trailblazers. Your work directly supports students as they discover their potential and develop into graduates who make a positive difference in the world. View Open Positions EMPLOYEE RESOURCES Benefits PC offers competitive health insurance, retirement contributions, tuition remission, and work-life balance in a supportive community where your contributions directly impact students’ transformational journeys. Employee Benefits New Employees EAP Employee Handbook Arts & Sciences Handbook A Culture of Respect At Presbyterian College, respect and just isn’t just a value—it’s our foundation. Our honor code creates a community where mutual dignity elevates everyone’s experience. This code transforms our campus into a place where integrity and justice become second nature, preparing graduates to lead with both excellence and character in a world hungry for ethical leadership and equitable systems. Title IX Bias Incident Report Holiday Schedule Fall 2026 Friday, July 3 Independence Day Monday, September 7 Labor Day Monday, October 12 Fall Break Wed-Fri, November 25-27 Thanksgiving Break* Mon-Thu, December 21-31 Christmas Break* Spring 2027 Fri, January 1 New Year’s Day Monday, January 18 Martin Luther King Day Friday, March 26 Good Friday Monday, May 31 Memorial Day Friday, June 18 Juneteenth Day More Holiday Info The Personnel Handbook recognizes certain holidays each academic year for full time staff employees. Some, but not all employees who have classifications other than full time will also receive the official paid days. Supervisors and employees should read the Personnel Handbook for staff’s eligibility to receive paid holidays. Please contact the Human Resource Office should you need additional information. The President and her Cabinet are pleased to announce that the 2026-2027 academic year holiday schedule will include extended days at Thanksgiving and Christmas. These extended days are for full time employees only. This larger block of holiday time will be determined each year by the President and the Leadership Team and should not be assumed to be an annual benefit. *Some full-time staff members will be required to work certain days during the extended holiday schedule, to cover essential duties , but they and their supervisor may, by prior agreement, substitute other days off so that each full-time staff member receives the same allotment of paid holidays. The substituted time off may not be extended into the next fiscal year nor may it be paid or taken at the rate of time and a half. Meet Our team Jean Copeland Assistant Director of Human Resources Operations [email protected] 864-833-8221 Sandy Dowdle Executive Director of Human Resources & Deputy Title IX Coordinator [email protected] 864-833-8207 Melissa Rhodes Administrative Assistant for Human Resources [email protected] (864) 938-3722 Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: 503 South Broad Street Clinton, South Carolina 29325 800.476.7272 Contact Us facebook instagram x flickr Quick Links & Resources Quick Links & Resources News Events Directory Athletics Campus Map Living on Campus Academic Calendar Course Catalog Offices & Facilities Accreditation Job Opportunities Justice & Community Wellbeing First-Gen Students International Students Accessible Education Health & Wellness Single-Sign On BannerWeb Brightspace Campus Bookstore Library Online Payment Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community Search for: © Copyright 2026 Presbyterian College | Title IX Policies Consumer Information Campus Police Presbyterian College is committed to providing an accessible and inclusive online experience. If you are unable to access any part of this website due to a disability, please contact Accessible Education at [email protected] for assistance. NOTICE OF NONDISCRIMINATORY POLICY AS TO STUDENTS: Presbyterian College is an equal educational opportunity institution. The College’s admission standards and practices are free from discrimination on the basis of age, sex, race, creed, color, disability, ethnicity or national origin. Apply Info Visit Give Search for: Resources For Close Menu Current Students Accepted Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends First-Gen Students Community"
